		{
			"id": "109314750611325839",
			"parentId": "109314735246007531",
			"url": "https://mas.to/@patak/109314731869283479",
			"author": {
				"name": "patak",
				"url": "https://mas.to/@patak",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/527/393/902/135/original/b698674a8671219e.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-09T16:13:55.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I would add that it would be great if not only we have plenty of successful frameworks to choose from, but also that we enter an era where we don't have a winner-take-all on building tools either. The webpack monopoly demiss shouldn't lead to another king being crowned. And we are good here too, with Vite, Rollup, and esbuild all growing strongly. Hopefully, we will see Parcel getting a lot more deserved usage. And even Turbopack playing along side the others.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
