			"parentId": "109314750611325839",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh/109314884578871714",
			"author": {
				"name": "Khalid ⚡",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/176/354/255/607/original/70d4899634530145.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-09T16:52:45.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mas.to/@patak\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>patak</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> from a developers perspective, a lot of teams are looking for the \"right\" answer. It's a internal challenge to not want your tech choice to dominate and validate your ego (right or wrong).</p><p>You folks are right in the sense that given better interoperability and lower barriers to switching between choices we'll have a healthier ecosystem.</p><p>The choices and conversations in the <a href=\"https://mastodon.social/tags/JavaScript\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>JavaScript</span></a> community are great and refreshing. Thank you two for being champions.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
